  "thesis": "Instability in lagged Bitcoin realized volatility may identify transition states with unusually uncertain risk. Reducing an otherwise passive unlevered BTC position from 100 percent to 50 percent only during high volatility-of-volatility percentile states may lower drawdown while preserving enough upside to improve fee-adjusted Calmar over passive BTC.",
  "economic_rationale": "Unlike volatility-level targeting, this policy responds only when the dispersion of log daily realized volatility is unusually high relative to its own trailing distribution. It is useful only if the state is not a repackaging of the closed volatility-level family and if partial de-risking improves direct matched-capital economics after fees, adverse slippage, annual path risk and terminal inventory accounting.",
