    "distinct_from_closed_families": [
      "The closed monthly 30-day volatility-target family continuously sized exposure as 0.40 divided by the current volatility level; this policy uses the dispersion of twenty log daily realized-volatility observations, percentile normalization, exactly two fixed weights and a frozen non-redundancy gate.",
      "The closed DRA realized-volatility family admitted or vetoed individual DRA entries; this policy has no DRA parent, no entry veto and instead partially rebalances a standalone passive BTC allocation.",
      "The closed VIX and SKEW families used external risk gauges and binary long-or-cash targets; this policy uses only sealed BTC hourly paths and never exits completely to cash.",
      "The open post-shock volatility family conditions on a three-percent event and awaits forward evidence; this policy uses every month boundary and no shock label."
    ],
    "redundancy_gate": "ABSOLUTE_SPEARMAN_CORRELATION_BETWEEN_MONTHLY_VOV_AND_20D_MEAN_DAILY_RV_AT_MOST_0_80_IN_BOTH_DESIGN_AND_VALIDATION",
